---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const updated = "11 July 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Talent — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Talent, the native Mac voice training and library app by DataIsland Software LLC, part of the PolySpeak suite."
>

  <section class="legal fade-in">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/privacy">← All Privacy Policies</a></div>

    <h1>Talent — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">DataIsland Software LLC &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      Talent is a native Mac voice training and voice library app, part of the PolySpeak
      voice-production suite. Because Talent trains AI voice models from recordings of
      real voices, this policy is deliberately direct about what the app does, what stays
      on your device, and where your responsibility as a user begins.
    </p>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Talent makes no network requests of any kind.</strong> Voice training and
      voice library management run entirely on your Mac using a local voice pipeline.
      Talent does use your microphone to record training samples, but only while you are
      actively recording, and only with your explicit permission. The app has no server,
      no account, and no analytics. Talent also asks you to attest to consent before
      training a voice — see "Consent Is Your Responsibility" below, which we consider
      the most important section of this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>What Talent Accesses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Microphone</strong> — used for recording training samples. This requires
        the standard macOS microphone permission prompt, and the microphone is only
        active while you are actively recording
      </li>
      <li>Audio files you explicitly import as training source material</li>
      <li>
        The local voice-library folder, where trained voice bundles are stored — model
        files, metadata, consent records, and resume/credit history
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Talent does not access your camera, contacts, location, photos, or calendar.
    </p>

    <h2>What Leaves Your Device</h2>

    <h3>Nothing</h3>
    <p>
      Voice training runs a local Python/RVC pipeline via subprocess entirely on your Mac.
      The recording used to train a voice, and the trained model itself, are never
      uploaded anywhere — never sent to DataIsland, and never sent to any third party.
      Everything Talent produces stays in your local voice library.
    </p>

    <h2>Consent Is Your Responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      Talent lets you train an AI voice model from a recording of someone's voice. This is
      powerful, and it can be misused. <strong>You must have the consent of the person
      whose voice you are recording and training a model from — or use only your own
      voice.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      Talent includes a consent-attestation step at training time, and the attestation is
      stored alongside the resulting voice bundle in your local voice library. But we want
      to be direct rather than defensive about the limits of that feature:
      <strong>DataIsland does not and cannot verify real-world consent.</strong> The
      attestation records that you affirmed you had consent at the time of training — it
      is not proof, and Talent has no way to confirm who actually spoke in a recording or
      whether that person actually agreed to it. That responsibility is yours, and it does
      not transfer to DataIsland by virtue of the attestation existing.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are training a voice model from someone else's recording — a collaborator, a
      voice actor, an interview subject, anyone — get their clear consent first, and keep
      your own record of it. See also the Terms of Use, which addresses the consequences of
      misusing voice-cloning technology.
    </p>

    <h2>What Is Stored Locally</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>The entire voice library</strong> — trained voice models, metadata, consent
        attestations, and resume/credit history, all in a local folder on your Mac
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>None of this data is synced to iCloud or any server — it stays in your local voice library.</p>

    <h2>What Talent Does Not Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Does not transmit any voice data or recordings anywhere</li>
      <li>Does not require an account or login</li>
      <li>Does not collect analytics, usage statistics, or crash reports</li>
      <li>Does not access your microphone except while you are actively recording</li>
      <li>Does not verify real-world consent — see above</li>
      <li>Does not share data with third parties</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Talent is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect
      information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we make material changes to this policy, we will update the "Last updated" date above.
      Continued use of Talent after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy:<br />
      <a href="mailto:support@dataisland.com">support@dataisland.com</a><br />
      DataIsland Software LLC
    </p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }

  .legal h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .meta { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2rem; }

  .legal h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .legal h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .legal p  { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }

  ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--gray-dark);
  }

  ul li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
